A||||12||anand||how fast will it go
Z||000000||anand||03-19-99||09:48 AM||||Some time ago I bought my first Fiero, which I almost immediatley started transforming into a Ferrari replica. At the time I bought the car I had only made a normal test drive. The car is a 2.8 V6. The speedometer displays a Vmax of some 80 mph. Does anyone know if this is normal? Could it be that the car was original a 4 cilinder and that this engine was swapped for the V6? More specific: the car is a 1985 4-speed.
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||03-19-99||12:06 PM||||Actually, and 80mph speedometer is normal for a Fiero V6. It's quite funny to see your speedometer go berzerk as soon as you hit around 90mph... You'd think you'd just entered the bermuda triangle!<p>You can buy some 120mph (which is about the top speed of a V6 automatic) conversion kits. Or you can go for a digital dash (yes, shameless plug intented!) which doesn't have a maxium and will display speeds up to however fast you can take it!<br>
Z||000002||black86gt||03-19-99||03:40 PM||||I don;t know about the bazerk thing at 80 mph but I have an 86 v6 with the 120 mph speedo.  It is stock on mine.  I have a gt by the way.  I did not know that any v6 came with the 80 mph speedo, thought they had the 120 but maybe they started that in 86?  As for the top speed, I have heard of several cases of fieros getting clocked at over 130 with the v6 stock.  I have never taken mine anywhere near that yet but it does not sound unreasonable to me.  Good luck with the kit...
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||03-19-99||04:22 PM||||Agreed, a stock Fiero with a low mileage engine can do around 130mph, a 5-stick can do even more than that but I'm not sure about the automatic though...<p>I've also seen a few stock Fieros with the 120mph speedometer but they seem very rare indeed. I was at a Fiero meeting last summer and there were about 100-150 Fieros there and only a few (that I'd seen) had 120mph Speedometers.
Z||000004||anand||03-20-99||02:53 AM||||So, it's quite normal! <p>Thanx
Z||000005||black86gt||03-21-99||08:45 PM||||SO my 120 mph speedo is a rare item?  I thought all at least 86+ gt cames with them.  no?
Z||000006||raceknb||03-26-99||10:12 PM||||I also have an 86 GT and also have the 120 speedo.  In stock form, I could get to 130 (because of a little thing called a Top Speed Limiter) that comes on some fo the 5speeds.  With a simple ADS chip change, the top speed limiter goes away. K&N Filter and open exhaust, and your Fiero should be able to come real close to 135.  Mine is a bit more built than that.<br>I run a race in Nevada called the Open Road Challange.  A 90 mile open Highway road race.<br>Wilth all the mods I have(and mind you  still street legal) Top speed of 149.782 miles per hour on the straight.  And thru the canyon at 130 which is 15 mph than the Saleen Mustang that started just ahead of me...
Z||000007||BlkFiero||04-07-99||01:40 AM||||I have a 88 coupe 4cyl 5 speed i estimate that I have done about 120 mph (I have the 85 mph speedo it has gone past the 85 mark and almost up to 0) the engine is stock. My Friend has a 88 formula with a 120 speedo and the one time I was following him he said he was doing 115. 
Z||000008||theogre||04-07-99||11:44 AM||||my 87 sc 4cyl has the 85 speedo burried by the time it hits 3500rpm. It had plenty of pedal left.
Z||000009||PaUL||04-09-99||06:15 PM||||I think the pre 86 SC v6 Fieros came with the 80mph speedos. Im talking about the ones that look like the original 2m4s but with a v6 and a 2m6 decal. I dont think these had the center console gauge pod either.
Z||000010||el loco||04-16-99||11:13 AM||||I have an 87 se with the v6.  It has a 120 speedo.  It's a 5 spd and will bury the speedo, but won't push past about 4 1/2 grand on the tach.  Think I need a good sized tune up.  I figure it should come close to about 135-140 mph if it can be pushed farther in 5th before redlining.
Z||000011||JT||05-01-99||02:36 PM||||Hello fellow Fiero owners.   This is my first time in this forum,, and it seems pretty cool so far.<br>I also have an '86 2m6  4-speed   with the 85 mph speedo.   But on the Freeway,, I have had the speedo well past the 85 mark.   I would estimate at least 115-120 mph..   And there was a lot of pedal left.<br>I'm in the process of ordering a rebuild kit for the v-6, and plan to add a crane compucam, and an ADS superchip.   The previous owner had the Cat- conv. removed   "no testing in my area".    
Z||000012||OilStumped||05-01-99||09:41 PM||||My 85 GT has an 80 mph speedo...and I've had it back to the zero...with no jumping around or anything like that though...once my tach hits about 5500 it goes a little nuts sometimes though...haha.  The 120 mph speedos and console gauges are for 86+ GT's only...I wonder if I could swap a set into my car though?
